  "worked_solution": "To find the absolute value of $-\\frac{13}{4},$ we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n|-\\frac{13}{4}|=\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/1cdef5eff1f2f6c70f18e29064fe7f32d0b63ba1e6ab91915d44ee8035dbafc8.png)",
